{"id": "sllama0237", "pool": "sllama", "arm": "aggressive", "tier": "aggressive", "lang": "en", "run_id": "ttfa1", "attempt": 1, "seed": 259608612, "protocol": "ttfa-v3", "config_sha256": "25e6887f8551649e559d24b54bbd2fe07f238cfc4d1ce1fc5ff87b67005b2d8d", "gate_art_sha256": "0e6494c2eeac9bcd86c10b5def3cbd32e98bb0765fa2fd8afc8c1b47915ea372", "threshold": 0.5533501505851746, "gpu": "NVIDIA H200", "host": "modal", "shard": 4, "query": "What is the smallest mammal?", "input_path": "/data/bench_audio/sllama0237.wav", "input_sha256": "28cc41d0cd47e9ce7c053298f8c3c5c1eb85c3678f006a19a59f85d26b217910", "input_samples": 31794, "input_s": 1.987, "n_real_chunks": 2, "score": 0.6153, "act": 0.999, "is_info": true, "fired": true, "mode": "escalated", "answer": "", "relay_text": "The smallest mammal by body mass is the Etruscan shrew (Suncus etruscus), weighing about 1.8 grams on average. The smallest mammal by skull/body length is often considered Kitti’s hog-nosed bat (Craseonycteris thonglongyai), also called the bumblebee bat.", "expert_answer": "The **smallest mammal by body mass** is the **Etruscan shrew** (*Suncus etruscus*), weighing about **1.8 grams** on average.\n\nThe **smallest mammal by skull/body length** is often considered **Kitti’s hog-nosed bat** (*Craseonycteris thonglongyai*), also called the **bumblebee bat**.", "transcript": "What is the smallest mammal?\n", "asr_s": 0.74, "expert_s": 2.77, "expert_input_samples": 31794, "expert_input_s": 1.987, "expert_input_sha256": "28cc41d0cd47e9ce7c053298f8c3c5c1eb85c3678f006a19a59f85d26b217910", "expert_timed_out": false, "wait_s": 0.265, "relay_synth_ms": 12578, "onset_chunk": 3, "eot_seen": true, "n_speak_chunks": 2, "feed_lag_max_ms": 1097, "feed_lag_sum_ms": 2163, "audio_files": {"relay": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/ttfa1/sllama/audio/sllama0237_aggressive_relay.wav", "sha256": "dc5efd4ec374bf2e3d15ccf4d6522b70a0b0ea3ff46159534201e97b837e2127", "sr": 24000, "seconds": 18.56}, "candidate": {"path": "/data/ttfa_real/t